* SN74ACT240N octal inverter, physical PDIP20 pin order.
* Functional approximation, NOT the unmodified TI SCAM124 macro.
* TI SCAM124 has 2.4e-5-ohm input resistors and an output inductor in parallel
* with its output resistance; neither is appropriate for this LTspice circuit.
* Nominal per-channel 9-ohm source/sink is a conservative approximation versus
* SCAM124's interpolated typical 6.17-ohm resistance at 5V; not a hardware guarantee.
* DRV_CORNER=1 selects 31-ohm source / 19-ohm sink as a resistance sensitivity test.
* TTL input threshold 1.4V, delay4ns plus0.1ns channel skew, 3p input, 7p output.
* Soft40mA current limit is an added modeling assumption, not actual silicon protection.
* Pins1/19 OE grounded. Channels1/2 invert RAW/DLY; remaining6 drive OUT1/2,
* three channels per output, identical inputs and OEs within this same package.
.subckt SN74ACT240N OE1 A11 Y24 A12 Y23 A13 Y22 A14 Y21 VN A21 Y14 A22 Y13 A23 Y12 A24 Y11 OE2 VP
X11 A11 Y11 OE1 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4n
X12 A12 Y12 OE1 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4.1n
X13 A13 Y13 OE1 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4.2n
X14 A14 Y14 OE1 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4.3n
X21 A21 Y21 OE2 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4n
X22 A22 Y22 OE2 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4.1n
X23 A23 Y23 OE2 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4.2n
X24 A24 Y24 OE2 VP VN ACT240_CHANNEL TD=4.3n
.ends
.subckt ACT240_CHANNEL A Y OE VP VN params: TD=4n
BA ALOG VN V=if(V(A,VN)>1.4,1,0)
BOEN EN VN V=if(V(OE,VN)<1.4,1,0)
AL ALOG EN VN VN VN NL NH VN AND Vhigh=1 Vlow=0 Td={TD} Trise=.6n Tfall=.6n
BH VP Y I=40m*V(NL,VN)*if(V(OE,VN)<1.4,1,0)*tanh(V(VP,Y)/({if(DRV_CORNER,31,9)}*40m))
BL Y VN I=40m*V(NH,VN)*if(V(OE,VN)<1.4,1,0)*tanh(V(Y,VN)/({if(DRV_CORNER,19,9)}*40m))
CA A VN 3p
CO Y VN 7p
.ends
